# Keep the build context small and the image clean.
_build/
deps/
.git/
.github/
.elixir_ls/

# Test + doc material not needed to build the release.
test/
docs/
*.md
.formatter.exs

# Local/editor cruft.
.env
erl_crash.dump

# Digested assets — regenerated by `mix assets.deploy` inside the builder, so shipping
# the local copies would only stale the context.
#
# **Scoped to `assets/`, and it has to be.** This was `priv/static/**/*-[0-9a-f]*.*`,
# which reads as "a hash suffix" and actually means "a hyphen followed by any of a-f or
# a digit, anywhere". `mix docs.publish` copies `docs/` and `ux/` under `priv/static`,
# so that rule dropped nine of them from the build context — seven design mocks,
# `design-brief.md` and `backend-capabilities.md` — and `COPY priv priv` could not bring
# in what the context never had. The image 404'd on files that were committed, present
# locally, and served fine in dev.
#
# The identical rule was in `.gitignore` and was fixed there first. This copy outlived
# it by a commit, which is the argument for `docs_served_test.exs` checking the published
# tree against **this file** rather than against a second reading of the same intent.
priv/static/cache_manifest.json
priv/static/assets/*-[0-9a-f]*.*
priv/static/**/*.gz

# The Claude session tooling.
.claude/
